  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "eof-modes-and-pdo-index",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/eof-modes-and-pdo-index.md",
      "sha256": "3544f2f552ecd0f41c41eb09edf7012f49ac8421900f2b571b8498d37f2726b1",
      "reason": "This fragment defines the PDO as the leading North Pacific SST EOF, with area-weighting, sign convention, explained-variance caveats, and amplitude/regression-pattern comparison, all central to the requested diagnostics.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Anomalies are SST minus the climatological annual cycle and minus the global-mean SST anomaly at each grid point; the EOF is taken on area-weighted data, weights `sqrt(cos(latitude))`; fix the sign so positive index = negative SST anomalies in the central and western North Pacific, and standardise the index (zero mean, unit variance).",
        "The EOF is dimensionless: report the mode's amplitude from the regression pattern (anomalies regressed on the standardised index, °C per standard deviation), and its area-weighted RMS in °C; compare explained variance only between fields on the same grid over the same period."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices.md",
      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The PDO anomalies must be formed relative to the specified 1950-2014 monthly climatology, and the fragment warns that baseline offsets and season definitions must not be mixed.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Take each source's anomaly against its **own** 1950-2014 monthly climatology (models and ERSSTv5 alike) so mean-state bias cancels, and state the baseline in the answer; an offset between series built on different baselines is not an error.",
        "A monthly index is matched against the climatology of its own calendar month, which removes the seasonal cycle; do not mix the DJF and JFM/AMJ/JAS/OND season conventions in one comparison."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The model-versus-ERSSTv5 regression-pattern correlations and regridded comparisons are only valid over cells where both fields have data after constructing and applying a common mask.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Masking a regression pattern to another source's coverage after the EOF does not make the patterns comparable: correlate each model's pattern with the ERSSTv5 pattern over the cells the two share (`analyze_correlation` leaves out cells either lacks, `weighting='area'`), and rank the models on those correlations.",
        "Report the shared-cell counts alongside the pattern correlations; a mask much smaller than the individual fields means the products disagree about where the ocean is, not that the models are poor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell.md",
      "sha256": "4acdeba0f49784d4435dbc4eed34ca9777254313daa951641759fa02df24cf64",
      "reason": "CMIP6 `tos` is top-cell bulk potential temperature rather than a skin temperature, so its definition and varying top-cell thickness affect comparison with ERSSTv5 SST.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`tos` is the bulk top-cell temperature including under sea ice (near-freezing values, not missing); `compute_pdo_index` takes the top level by default (`depth_level=None`) — a `depth_level` of 10 m is not the same quantity across these models.",
        "Never give a model index an observed climatology (`climatology='woa23'`): that puts the model's mean-state bias into the index."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The EOF variance, amplitude, and persistence are computed from monthly mean fields, and the fragment warns that nonlinear diagnostics from monthly averages can differ from time-step-derived quantities.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The 1950-2014 monthly climatology is the plain mean of each calendar month across the years, as climate normals are defined; day weights do not enter it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "The requested bilinear regridding changes land-sea masks and conservation properties, so it is appropriate for pattern comparisons but must be handled consistently when computing EOFs and patterns.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "An EOF mode with its explained variance and regression pattern depends on the grid: put all four sources, observations included, on the one 1° grid before the analysis and take every reported number there, with `regrid_horizontal` method `'bilinear'` as the question specifies — state the method."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "serial-correlation-and-significance",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/serial-correlation-and-significance.md",
      "sha256": "fe11bd008257a589f44e369faba5fa31ab3cf9ad99280e88c763ac45d2b0e917",
      "reason": "The lag-1-year autocorrelation and correlation with the published PDO involve strongly autocorrelated monthly series, so effective sample size and significance should not be treated naively.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Correlate the ERSSTv5-derived index with the published PDO as it is (no `detrend`): the shared trend is part of the agreement being checked; quote the effective-sample-size-corrected significance that `analyze_correlation` returns by default.",
        "No correction exists for a pattern correlation across space: read its coefficient, not its p-value; the 12-month lag autocorrelation is the persistence figure to report as is."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245",
